  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Deflection maximum is grid-limited: per unit alpha 18.83 at b=0.739/(ef) reported, true maximum 18.8586 at b=0.7743/(ef) (two gauges agree to 4e-5). Physical: 6.6e-39 rad at 0.41 fm -> 6.61e-39 rad at 0.43 fm (f=64.5 MeV); 1.35e-38 rad at 0.29 fm -> 1.35e-38 at 0.30 fm (f=92.2 MeV).",
   "suggested_fix": "Refine the maximum (bounded scalar maximisation) instead of taking the largest of 60 geometric grid points; quote 18.86 at b=0.77/(ef), 0.43 fm and 0.30 fm."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "'The physical coupling is 39 orders of magnitude below alpha_crit': alpha_crit/alpha_phys = 1.15e38, i.e. 38 orders (alpha_phys/alpha_crit = 8.7e-39 = 10^-38.06).",
   "suggested_fix": "Say 38 orders of magnitude (or quote the ratio 8.7e-39)."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Seed verdict 'commitment 5 AMENDED' attributes the failure of the PLAN's Newtonian -1/2 int rho Phi expectation to the seed. SEED section 5 already identifies 'energy bends the cone' with GR (Weinberg/Deser), whose source is the full T_mu_nu; the computation solves GR by construction, so the seed's physics is not corrected, only its plain-language gloss. The MISS belongs to the preregistered prediction.",
   "suggested_fix": "Keep the MISS on the PLAN prediction; give commitment 5 'CONFIRMED (GR by construction), wording clarified: stress-energy, not energy density alone, sources the metric', or mark the AMENDED as wording-only."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Verdict words on by-construction identities: M_ADM(alpha->0)/E_flat = 1 is labelled CALIBRATED (there is no literature target) and the 4GM/b deflection is CONFIRMED with no 'by construction' caveat in seed_claims (the EP entry does carry the caveat).",
   "suggested_fix": "Label these 'consistency check (by construction)'; add the caveat to the SEED 5 light-bending entry."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Provenance: the report says PLAN.md section 4 E6 'asks four things' including a stability question with a 'literature note: the upper branch is unstable', light deflection, Shapiro delay and an f = 92.2 MeV case. PLAN.md E6 contains only calibration, the EP check and the physical-scale metric deviation; the rest are additions (welcome ones) that should be labelled as such, and 'upper branch unstable' is not a seed claim.",
   "suggested_fix": "Mark stability, deflection, Shapiro delay and f = 92.2 MeV as extensions beyond PLAN E6, and move the stability verdict out of seed_claims."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "The exchange-energy table presents the cancellation of the p_ij p'_ij and -1/2 p p' terms (to 5e-8) as a numerical finding. For any static, conserved (d_i p_ij = 0), spherically symmetric stress the Fourier-space stress is pure transverse trace, A(k)(delta_ij - k_i k_j), for which p_ij p_ij - p^2/2 = 0 identically; the individual values (+-0.6765) carry no separate meaning.",
   "suggested_fix": "State the identity; quote only the rho-rho and rho-p terms."
  }
